# Reviewed checksums for the two artifacts the build starts from.
#
# The build already checked each download against the checksum the vendor
# publishes NEXT TO the file. That proves the transfer was not corrupted; it
# proves nothing about the artifact. If upstream replaces the file, the
# published checksum is replaced with it and the check still passes.
#
# These values are pinned here instead: reviewed once, committed, and compared
# on every build. They are the exact bytes that produced the image published
# on 2026-09-03 (sha256 a301f6a8...), which is the strongest provenance this
# project can offer -- not "what the server served today" but "what the image
# people downloaded was actually built from".
#
# Arch Linux ARM rebuilds its rootfs every few weeks, so this WILL stop
# matching. That is the point: the build stops and a person looks, instead of
# silently absorbing a new artifact. Refresh with:
#
#   scripts/update-base-image-pins.sh
#
# Proposed by Fail-Safe in PR #6. The two values below were computed
# independently here and match that PR exactly.
c81699152db11d2a6dbb7d75348d632fcf5811eff414d7e71876a8bb6d48bc02  alpine-virt-3.24.1-aarch64.iso
42a4eeaa038994ffd31fa173256ef2f0ef511358eeb41b9ea1f8626391b9b319  ArchLinuxARM-aarch64-latest.tar.gz
